\p \v 10 \w As the cloud|strong="H06051"\w* \w lifted|strong="H05493"\w* \w from above|strong="H05921"\w* \w the Tent|strong="H00168"\w*, \w suddenly|strong="H02009"\w* \w Miriam|strong="H04813"\w* \w [became] leprous|strong="H06879"\w*,\f + \fr 12:10 \ft The Hebrew word traditionally translated as \fqa leprous \ft was used for various skin diseases; see Leviticus 13.\f* \w [white] as snow|strong="H07950"\w*. \w Aaron|strong="H00175"\w* \w turned|strong="H06437"\w* \w toward|strong="H00413"\w* \w her|strong="H04813"\w*, \w saw that|strong="H02009"\w* \w she [was] leprous|strong="H06879"\w*, \v 11 \w and said|strong="H00559"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00175"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H04872"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H00994"\w* “\w My lord|strong="H00113"\w*, \w please|strong="H04994"\w* \w do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w hold|strong="H07896"\w* \w against us|strong="H05921"\w* \w this sin|strong="H02403"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w we have so foolishly|strong="H02973"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w committed|strong="H02398"\w*. \v 12 \w Please|strong="H04994"\w* \w do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w let her be|strong="H01961"\w* \w like a stillborn infant|strong="H04191"\w* \w whose|strong="H00834"\w* \w flesh|strong="H01320"\w* \w is half|strong="H02677"\w* \w consumed|strong="H00398"\w* \w when he comes out|strong="H03318"\w* \w of his mother’s|strong="H00517"\w* \w womb|strong="H07358"\w*.”
