\s1 Laws about Offerings
\p \v 1 \w Then the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w said|strong="H01696"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H04872"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w*, \v 2 “\w Speak|strong="H01696"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H01121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03478"\w* \w and tell them|strong="H00559"\w*: \w After|strong="H03588"\w* \w you enter|strong="H00935"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w am giving|strong="H05414"\w* you \w as a home|strong="H04186"\w* \v 3 \w and you present|strong="H06213"\w* \w a food offering|strong="H00801"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w from|strong="H04480"\w* \w the herd|strong="H01241"\w* \w or|strong="H00176"\w* \w . . .|strong="H04480"\w* \w flock|strong="H06629"\w* \w to produce|strong="H06213"\w* \w a pleasing|strong="H05207"\w* \w aroma|strong="H07381"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* — \w either a burnt offering|strong="H05930"\w* \w or|strong="H00176"\w* \w a sacrifice|strong="H02077"\w*, \w for a special|strong="H06381"\w* \w vow|strong="H05088"\w* \w or|strong="H00176"\w* \w freewill offering|strong="H05071"\w* \w or|strong="H00176"\w* \w appointed feast|strong="H04150"\w*— \v 4 \w then the one presenting|strong="H07126"\w* \w his offering|strong="H07133"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w shall also present|strong="H07126"\w* \w a grain offering|strong="H04503"\w* \w of a tenth of an ephah|strong="H06241"\w* \w of fine flour|strong="H05560"\w*\f + \fr 15:4 \fqa A tenth of an ephah \ft is approximately 2 dry quarts or 2.2 liters (probably about 2.6 pounds or 1.2 kilograms of flour).\f* \w mixed|strong="H01101"\w* \w with a quarter|strong="H07243"\w* \w hin|strong="H01969"\w* \w of olive oil|strong="H08081"\w*.\f + \fr 15:4 \ft Or \fqa a quarter hin of oil\ft ; that is, approximately 0.97 quarts or 0.92 liters; similarly in verse 5\f* \v 5 \w With|strong="H05921"\w* \w the burnt offering|strong=